.TH MWFORMAT 1
.SH NAME
mwformat \- format a Morrow HD\-DMA hard disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mwformat
device [ track ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I mwformat
runs the controller's format\-track command across a drive, one track per
ioctl, printing a line as each track is done.  The device node names the
drive and the model (its minor number); the model's geometry is how many
tracks are walked.  A format blanks the disk \- headers and data \- so the
label and any filesystem go with it, and
.IR mkfs (1)
follows.
.PP
With a
.I track
argument, only that one track is formatted.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B mwformat /dev/m16a
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mkfs(1)
